<BlogPost
  title="Horizontal vs. Vertical Grain: How to Order Metropolitan and Napa Doors"
  description="Metropolitan and Napa are the two Shiloh and Eclipse door styles offered in horizontal or vertical grain. Order codes, which parts actually change grain direction, height limits by species, and how to get horizontal grain on cabinet sides."
  author="Ben Miller"
  publishedDate="2026-06-09"
  ogImage="/images/blog/horizontal-grain-metro-napa-doors/listing-card.webp"
>

<p>Horizontal grain is one of the fastest ways to make a slab or slim-shaker kitchen read modern — a long, unbroken grain line across a run of drawers and doors. Shiloh and Eclipse offer it, but only on two door styles, and there are a few rules that affect the drawings. Here's everything you need before you quote it.</p>

<h2>Which door styles</h2>

<p>Horizontal and vertical grain options are available on <strong>Metropolitan</strong> and <strong>Napa</strong> door styles <strong>only</strong>. To specify, select the door and drawer style on your <strong>Order Cover Sheet</strong> or in <strong>2020 Design Flex</strong>:</p>

<div class="spec-table-wrap">
  <table class="spec-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Vertical grain</th><th scope="col">Horizontal grain</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Door</th><td>METRO-V / NAPA-V</td><td>METRO-H / NAPA-H</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Drawer head</th><td>DF-METRO-V / DF-NAPA-V</td><td>DF-METRO-H / DF-NAPA-H</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>The newer <a href="/playbook/pacifica-ventura-door-styles/">Pacifica and Ventura</a> styles also offer vertical or horizontal grain on their <em>drawer fronts</em>; see that post for their rules.</p>

<h2>Rules that change your drawings</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Horizontal grain applies to doors, drawer fronts, and decorative door end panels only.</strong> Cabinet finished ends stay <strong>vertical grain</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Want horizontal grain on the cabinet sides?</strong> Use <strong>Decorative Door End Panels</strong> — that's the recommended way to carry the horizontal look around an island or the end of a run.</li>
  <li><strong>Some height SKUs aren't available in vertical-grain cabinetry.</strong> Check the individual cabinet page in the spec book before you lock the elevation.</li>
  <li><strong>Size limits on horizontal-grain doors.</strong> Horizontal-grain Metro and Napa doors aren't available above the sizes in the table below. If you go above them, the door is built as <strong>two doors pinned together</strong> with a standard reveal (3/16″ gap) between them — which interrupts the continuous grain line your client is paying for. Design around it, or show the client the seam in the drawings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Horizontal-grain door height availability</h2>

<div class="spec-table-wrap">
  <table class="spec-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Species / material</th><th scope="col">Up to 48″ tall</th><th scope="col">Up to 60″ tall</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Alder</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Cherry</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Hickory</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">HPL</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Maple</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Red Oak</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">S.A. Poplar</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Walnut</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Recon. Walnut</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Recon. White Oak</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Qtr. Sawn White Oak</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Rift Cut White Oak</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">TFL</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">PV</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>Bottom line: in real wood species, plan horizontal-grain doors at <strong>48″ tall or less</strong>. HPL and TFL go to 60″. Tall pantry doors above those heights will be split into two pinned doors.</p>

